📈 Graph Plotter (Python)

A collection of mathematical graph visualisations built using Python, NumPy, and Matplotlib.
This project explores different types of equations including standard functions, parametric curves, and implicit equations.

✨ Features
📉 Linear graphs
📊 Quadratic and cubic functions
📈 Exponential growth
🔄 Reciprocal functions (with asymptotes)
⚪ Parametric circle
❤️ Heart curve (implicit equation)
🦋 Butterfly curve (parametric / polar)
🧠 What this project demonstrates

This project shows three key ways of plotting mathematical functions:

1. Standard Functions

Functions of the form:

y = f(x)

Example:

Linear
Quadratic
Cubic
2. Parametric Equations

Points are generated using a parameter t:

x = f(t)
y = g(t)

Example:

Circle
Butterfly curve
3. Implicit Equations

Equations where x and y are combined:

f(x, y) = 0

These are plotted by testing a grid of values and drawing where the equation equals zero.

Example:

Heart curve
🛠️ Technologies Used
Python 3
NumPy
Matplotlib
▶️ How to Run
Install dependencies:
pip install numpy matplotlib
Run the script:
python graph_plotter.py
